---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { site, fullAddress } from "../lib/site";

const toc = [
  { id: "who-we-are", label: "Who we are" },
  { id: "what-we-collect", label: "What we collect" },
  { id: "health-information", label: "Health information" },
  { id: "how-we-use", label: "How we use it" },
  { id: "cookies", label: "Cookies and choices" },
  { id: "third-parties", label: "Other services" },
  { id: "sharing", label: "Sharing" },
  { id: "hipaa", label: "Your medical records" },
  { id: "keeping-safe", label: "Keeping it safe" },
  { id: "your-rights", label: "Your rights" },
  { id: "children", label: "Children" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact us" },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Mercy Family Clinic collects, uses and protects information on this website, in plain words."
  updated="October 6, 2026"
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="who-we-are" data-reveal>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website belongs to <strong>{site.name}</strong>, a family medicine clinic at {fullAddress}.
      This policy explains what we do with information when you use this website.
      It is written in simple words on purpose.
    </p>
    <p>
      It covers this website only. Your care at the clinic and your medical records are covered separately (see{" "}
      <a href="#hipaa">Your medical records</a>).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what-we-collect" data-reveal>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <h3>What you tell us</h3>
    <p>When you use our appointment request form, we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your full name and phone number (required)</li>
      <li>Your email address (optional)</li>
      <li>Your reason for visit and preferred day (reason is chosen from a list, day is optional)</li>
      <li>Any message you choose to write</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The form sends this to the clinic by email so our team can call you. We use it for that purpose only.</p>
    <h3>What your browser shares automatically</h3>
    <p>
      Like every website, our web host may keep standard server logs, such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you
      asked for. We use these only to keep the site secure and working.
    </p>
    <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
    <p>We do not use advertising trackers. We do not use analytics tools at this time. We do not sell your information.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="health-information" data-reveal>
    <h2>Please do not send health details through the website</h2>
    <p>
      The contact form and email are <strong>not a secure way</strong> to share medical information. Please do not write your symptoms,
      test results, medicines or other private health details in the form. Call us at <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> and
      our team will help you safely.
    </p>
    <p><strong>If this is an emergency, call 911.</strong> Do not use this website.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-we-use" data-reveal>
    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To answer your request and book your visit</li>
      <li>To reply to questions you send us</li>
      <li>To keep this website safe, fast and working well</li>
      <li>To follow the law when we have to</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies" data-reveal>
    <h2>Cookies and your choices</h2>
    <p>
      A cookie is a small file a website saves on your device. We keep cookies to a minimum. When you first visit, a banner asks for
      your choice. You can change your mind at any time with the{" "}
      <button type="button" data-cookie-settings class="font-medium text-brand-700 underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-900">Cookie settings</button>{" "}
      button here or in the footer of every page.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">How long</th><th scope="col">Type</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>mfc_consent</td>
          <td>Remembers your cookie choice (set by us)</td>
          <td>About 6 months</td>
          <td>Essential, always on</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Google Maps</td>
          <td>Shows the interactive map on our contact area. Google may set its own cookies. It loads only if you allow it or press "Load map".</td>
          <td>Set by Google. See Google's policy.</td>
          <td>Optional, off until you agree</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      You can also delete cookies in your browser settings. If you do, the banner will ask again.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-parties" data-reveal>
    <h2>Other services this website uses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Maps</strong> shows our location, only with your permission. When it loads, Google receives your IP address and
        browser details. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Form delivery service.</strong> We use a service that carries your form message to the clinic's email.
        It handles your message only to deliver it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Stock photos.</strong> Some pictures load from Unsplash's servers. As with any image, their servers can see
        your IP address when your browser fetches a picture. We do not use these requests to track you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Links to other sites</strong> (for example our Google reviews). Those sites have their own privacy rules.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing" data-reveal>
    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>We do not sell or rent your information. We share it only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>With the companies that help us run this website and deliver your messages (they may use it only for that work)</li>
      <li>When the law requires it, for example a valid court order</li>
      <li>To protect people's safety or to stop fraud or misuse of this website</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="hipaa" data-reveal>
    <h2>Your medical records</h2>
    <p>
      Information about your health and care at our clinic is protected by the federal law called HIPAA and by Texas medical records
      privacy law. How we use and share that information is explained in our{" "}
      <strong>Notice of Privacy Practices</strong>. Ask our front desk for a copy, or call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      As a patient you have rights over your medical records, including the right to ask to see them, to ask for corrections, and to
      ask how they have been shared. Please ask our team to use these rights. This website is not the place to do that.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="keeping-safe" data-reveal>
    <h2>Keeping it safe</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable steps to protect information we receive through this website, including encrypted (HTTPS) connections.
      No website can promise perfect security, which is why we ask you not to send health details online. We keep appointment
      requests only as long as we need them to schedule your visit and meet our legal duties.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-rights" data-reveal>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>For information you gave us through this website, you can ask us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Tell you what we hold about you</li>
      <li>Correct anything that is wrong</li>
      <li>Delete it, unless the law says we must keep it</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can also change your cookie choice at any time. To make a request, contact us using the details below.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="children" data-reveal>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This website is for adults. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13 through the website. Parents and
      guardians are welcome to call us to book visits for their children.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes" data-reveal>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of the page shows when it last changed. If we make big changes,
      we will tell you on this website.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" data-reveal>
    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy? We are happy to help.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>{site.name}</strong>, {fullAddress}</li>
      <li>Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> · Fax: {site.fax}</li>
      <li>Or use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> (please do not include health details)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
